{{also|Appendix:Variations of "bara"}}
==Swedish==

===Etymology===
{{root|sv|ine-pro|*bʰer-}}
From {{inh|sv|gmq-osw|bæra}}, from {{inh|sv|non|bera}}, from {{inh|sv|gem-pro|*beraną}}, from {{der|sv|ine-pro|*bʰer-}} (whence also {{l|sv|börja}}, {{l|sv|bår}} and {{l|sv|barn}}). Cognate with {{cog|da|bære}}, {{cog|no|bære}}, and {{cog|en|bear}}.<ref>{{R:runeberg.org|svetym|0166.html bära}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|sv|Sv-bära.ogg|audio}}

===Verb===
{{sv-verb-irr|bär|bar|burit|bär}}

# to [[carry]]; to lift and transport anywhere else
#* {{quote-book|sv|year=1914|author={{w|Dan Andersson}}|title=[http://runeberg.org/dansamsk/1/ Kolarhistorier]|chapter=Utrivning|pageurl=http://runeberg.org/dansamsk/1/0112.html|page=34
|passage=Isen var så tjock och där var så djupt till vattnet att man fick ställa sig på knä i snön för att ösa upp vatten i hinken. <br>Två sådana fans, vi '''buro''' upp dem fulla och ställde dem ett stycke från milan.|t=The ice there was so thick and it was so deep to the water that one had to get down on ones knees in the snow, to scoop up water into the bucket. <br>There were two of those, and we '''carried''' them filled and put them down a bit away from the charcoal pile.}}
# to [[wear]]; e.g. a piece of clothing or jewelry
# {{lb|sv|often with a particle like {{m|sv|upp}}}} to [[support]], to [[bear]]
#: {{ux|sv|Taket '''bärs upp''' av pelare|The roof '''is supported''' by columns}}
#: {{ux|sv|Jag hoppas isen '''bär'''|I hope the ice '''will carry us (be able to support us)'''}}
# {{lb|sv|often|impersonal}} to [[head]]
#: {{ux|sv|Imorgon '''bär''' det av (till Säffle)!|Tomorrow we're (setting) off (to Säffle)! ("Tomorrow it '''heads''' off (to Säffle)!")}}
#: {{ux|sv|En bit fram '''bär''' vägen utför|A little further on, the road goes downhill ("A bit forth the road '''heads''' downhill")}}
#: {{ux|sv|Vem vet var det '''bär''' {{l|sv|hän}}?|Who knows where it will lead? ("Who knows where it '''heads''' away (to)?)}}

